# Verification before "done"

Do not say "fixed", "ready", "passing", or "done" without running the matching gate and reading its output.

## Pick the narrowest gate

| Touched files | Run |
|---------------|-----|
| `src/web/**/*.{ts,tsx,css}` only | `cd src/web && pnpm check` (Biome + ESLint + tsc + Vitest) |
| `src/tauri/**/*.rs` or `src/agent/**/*.rs` only | `make lint-rust` then `make test` (or the `rust-validate` skill) |
| Both stacks, or unsure | `make check` then `make test-all` |
| Docs / rules / Make / scripts only | None required, unless a script changed CI behavior |

## Mandatory before commit

Before committing in Cursor, run the gate above manually, paste the relevant pass/fail line into the assistant message, then commit.

## What "evidence" means

Quote the actual command and the **exit code or last line of output**. "I ran the tests" without output is not evidence.
